<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Provence</h1><p class="st-meta">855 CE – 863 CE · capital Vienne</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived Carolingian kingdom of the lower Rhône, carved out for the youngest son of Lothair I.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair I</a> divided <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/middle-francia">Middle Francia</a> in 855, his youngest son Charles, still a boy, received <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-provence">Provence</a> and the duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a>, stretching from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> valley.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Charles suffered from epilepsy, and the kingdom was effectively run by Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerard-of-roussillon">Girart of Vienne</a>, his guardian, who defended it against the ambitions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raiders who had sailed up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a> were its main centres.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Charles died childless in 863, and his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-ii">Lothair II</a> and the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ii-of-italy">Louis II</a> divided the kingdom between them. The region later re-emerged as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-lower-burgundy">Kingdom of Lower Burgundy</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boso-of-provence">Boso</a> in 879.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-provence.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Provence" width="320" height="340"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (Sidonius) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Hoch_und_Niederburgund_EN.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>855 CE – 863 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vienne</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles of Provence, Girart of Vienne</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin, Old Occitan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Provence (855-863)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=859&amp;focus=kingdom-of-provence" aria-label="Kingdom of Provence on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4824 619 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Provence lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5144 875L5139 672"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5139 672h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5144 875h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5144 875h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=859&amp;focus=kingdom-of-provence">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
